/-!
# Whole-lattice weak Fourier limit generated by an infinite shell lineage

An actual infinite source lineage with one strict critical margin generates
physical punctured-cube Galerkin trajectories on every requested finite time
interval.  Whole-carrier compactness selects one strictly monotone
subsequence.  Punctured-cube exhaustion survives that reindexing, and the
complete infinite nonlinear row passes to the same whole-state limit.

The resulting state limit satisfies the distributional vorticity equation
at every nonzero Fourier wave and for every endpoint-zero `C¹` time test.
Neither a trajectory sequence, a Cauchy witness, a target limit, nor mode
coverage is supplied in the theorem mouth.
-/

